  "title": "dumpcap: clean up capture_loop_init_output().",
  "description": "Instead of doing\n\n\tattempt to open file for writing;\n\tif (open for writing succeeded) {\n\t\twrite out initial records;\n\t\tif (writes failed) {\n\t\t\tclose file;\n\t\t\tmake it look as if open for writing failed;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif (open for writing failed) {\n\t\treport error;\n\t}\n\ndo\n\n\tattempt to open file for writing;\n\tif (open for writing failed) {\n\t\treport open error and return error indication;\n\t}\n\twrite out initial records;\n\tif (writes failed) {\n\t\treport write error;\n\t\tclose file;\n\t\treturn;\n\t}\n\nas that reports the two issues differently, and is a bit cleaner.",
